---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const steps = [
  ['Talk', 'We learn what the business actually needs, who the site is for and what success should look like.'],
  ['Build', 'A focused first version is designed and built quickly, with clear feedback points instead of endless meetings.'],
  ['Launch', 'We publish, connect the domain and make sure the finished site is fast, responsive and easy to live with.']
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Avocado Signal"
  description="Meet Ivan, the person behind Avocado Signal, and discover a straightforward approach to useful, lightweight websites."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <section class="founder-hero shell">
    <div class="founder-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Meet the person behind Avocado Signal</p>
      <h1>A small studio.<br /><span>A real person.</span></h1>
      <p class="founder-lead">Hi, I’m Ivan. I created Avocado Signal to give small businesses straightforward, professional websites without agency jargon, inflated fees or unnecessary complexity.</p>
      <p>You deal directly with me from the first conversation to the finished site. No account manager, no mysterious handover and no need to learn a new dialect of digital marketing.</p>
      <div class="founder-actions">
        <a
          class="button button-primary"
          href="https://wa.me/97471670038?text=Hi%20Ivan%2C%20I%27d%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20website."
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >Message Ivan on WhatsApp</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@avocadosignal.co.uk">Or send an email <span>→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="founder-portrait">
      <img
        src="/ivan-founder.webp"
        alt="Ivan Langton, founder of Avocado Signal"
        width="960"
        height="1317"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Ivan Langton</strong>
        <span>Founder, designer and your actual point of contact.</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="manifesto">
    <div class="shell manifesto-grid">
      <p class="section-kicker">The thinking behind it</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Your website should help your business.<br />Not become another job.</h2>
        <p>I’ve spent years working where technology meets real people. The useful lesson is that the cleverest solution is rarely the one with the most moving parts. It is the one people understand, trust and can actually use.</p>
        <p>Small businesses are routinely sold websites with more machinery than they need. I prefer to start with the customer, the message and the action the site needs to support. Everything else has to earn its place.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell split-section about-split">
    <div class="eco-panel">
      <p class="section-kicker light">Lighter by design</p>
      <h2>Efficiency is part of the design, not an afterthought.</h2>
      <p>Every website uses energy. We reduce avoidable data transfer and computing through static pages, compressed assets and minimal third-party code. Those choices usually make a site faster and simpler too.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Static-first architecture</li>
        <li>Optimised assets</li>
        <li>Minimal third-party scripts</li>
        <li>Efficient global delivery</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="eco-transparency"><strong>What we do not claim:</strong> “tread lightly” does not mean zero emissions, carbon neutral or green-hosted. It is a practical commitment to reduce what we can, explain what we do and avoid claims we cannot evidence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="process-panel">
      <p class="section-kicker">How we work</p>
      <div class="steps">
        {steps.map(([title, text], index) => (
          <div class="step">
            <span>0{index + 1}</span>
            <div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles shell">
    <p class="section-kicker">A few rules we like</p>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article><h3>Clarity beats cleverness.</h3><p>People should understand what a business does before they have time to admire the animation.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Speed is a feature.</h3><p>A page that arrives quickly is better for customers, search engines and the amount of infrastructure needed to serve it.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Own less technology.</h3><p>If a simple static site solves the problem, we will not invent a reason to add a database, CMS or plugin stack.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta shell" id="contact">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker light">Sound like your sort of approach?</p>
      <h2>Let’s give your business a signal.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="button button-light" href="mailto:hello@avocadosignal.co.uk">Email Ivan</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
